<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by an assertion failure in the QuickJS library. The `JS_AddIntrinsicTypedArrays` function, when called, also calls `JS_AddIntrinsicAtomics`. This second function attempts to define a property named "Atomics" on the global object. However, if this property already exists, the library intentionally aborts.

The fuzz driver calls `JS_AddIntrinsicTypedArrays` which is a valid API call. The underlying project code does not handle being called multiple times gracefully. This is a bug in the project.

A potential patch for the project would be to add a check in `JS_AddIntrinsicAtomics` to see if the "Atomics" property already exists before attempting to define it. For example:

```c
void JS_AddIntrinsicAtomics(JSContext *ctx)
{
JSValue atomics = JS_GetPropertyStr(ctx, ctx->global_obj, "Atomics");
if (JS_IsUndefined(atomics)) {
/* add Atomics as autoinit object */
JS_SetPropertyFunctionList(ctx, ctx->global_obj, js_atomics_obj, countof(js_atomics_obj));
}
JS_FreeValue(ctx, atomics);
}
```
This would make the function idempotent and prevent the crash.
</crash-analysis>

